    "title": "Kennedy Space Center to unveil Artemis II exhibit",
    "text": "Kennedy Space Center Visitor Complex has added an exhibit named “Artemis II: Pathway to the Moon”. The NASA displays include authentic Artemis hardware, a 14-foot moon replica and other large-scale models, a crew showcase featuring personal items and an examination of spacesuits and tools for future missions. The exhibit is located on the ground floor of the Space Shuttle Atlantis attraction. Visitors can follow the flight path and explore technologies and the teams that are making the country’s return to the Moon possible. The Brevard County-based attraction also features a series of 25-minute presentations in the Journey to Mars area during the upcoming launch week of Artemis II. They will be led by experts tied to Orion spacecraft, exploration ground systems, NASA’s Human Research Program and Science Mission Directorate. Artemis commercial partners will be represented at Inside Gateway: The Deep Space Launch Complex. All “Artemis: Pathway to the Moon” activities are included with regular Kennedy Space Center Visitor Complex admission. But dates and hours are subject to change based on Artemis II launch windows. Currently, the mission will launch no earlier than April 1. On launch-attempt days, only guests with an Artemis II Launch Viewing Package — which are sold out — will be permitted to enter the visitor complex. For more information, go to kennedyspacecenter.com. For NASA launch announcements and updates, go to nasa.gov/missions/artemis-ii. Your guide to exploring the region: Sign up to the Explore Florida & the Caribbean weekly newsletter.By signing up, you agree to our Terms of Use, Privacy Policy, and to receive emails from Sun Sentinel.dbevil@orlandosentinel.com RevContent Feed",
